[0.1.0]
* Initial package of opendesk at upstream commit 898e594
* Cloudron single sign-on, Cloudron mail relay for platform email
* Mailboxes on the Cloudron mail server connect over the internal network
* Mailbox wizard recommends Email password and hides forwarding, which needs an inbound route this package does not provide
* AI setup guide: hosted providers, NanoGPT, or private local models with LM Studio over NetBird
* App store description, setup guide and five listing screenshots

[0.1.1]
* Link the Cloudron forum topic for questions and feedback
* No change to the app; opendesk is still at upstream commit 898e594

[0.1.2]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit bb2b56b
* Unified customer email templates, team and agent signatures, per-brand email designs and satisfaction emails, with live previews and template helpers
* Integration and import-source logos, updated AI defaults and reply guidance, and upstream dependency updates
* Keep the Cloudron base image and existing SSO and mail patches unchanged

[0.1.3]
* Fix IMAP mailboxes that stopped syncing after their first pass: a finished sync no longer blocks the next one-minute poll (upstream fix 9c7cc1a)
* Update opendesk to upstream commit f9471ba
* Let admins copy and resend invitation links
* Include upstream update-status support; Cloudron remains responsible for package updates, with no upstream self-updater installed
* Include upstream Collab mail accounts, integration sign-in support, and database migrations
* Name newly connected Gmail accounts from the Google profile, falling back to the Gmail send-as name
* Refresh the forwarding-disabled mailbox UI patch for upstream's Collab connection options
* Keep the Cloudron base image, SSO and internal mail routing unchanged

[0.2.0]
* Help centers on your own domain: add an alias such as help.example.com to the app, then connect it to a brand in opendesk
* A wildcard alias such as *.help.example.com gives every brand's help center its own subdomain, <slug>.help.example.com
* Cloudron issues the certificates; mail addresses are unaffected
* Fix help centers at /help/<slug>, which showed the opendesk app instead of the help center
* No change to opendesk itself; it is still at upstream commit f9471ba

[0.2.1]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit 809b80d
* Include upstream session, sign-in, webhook and inbound-email security controls
* Add side conversations, browser and Web Push notifications, and chat-widget voice messages and attachment controls
* Include import threading improvements, editing and deleting internal notes, and changing a ticket's contact
* Include resumable attachment imports, NUL-safe imports, shared reply drafts, chat intro settings and Azerbaijani language support
* Send platform mail through authenticated SMTPS with verified server certificates, compatible with upstream production security validation
* Update the pinned Cloudron base to 6.0.1 with its patched CA bundle; keep SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support
* Fix mailbox setup offering email forwarding when the server has no inbound route; the wizard now says when no receiving method is available

[0.2.2]
* Fix platform email (invitations, sign-in links, password resets, notifications) timing out in 0.2.1
* Send through Cloudron's mail relay with STARTTLS, the port Cloudron forwards for the mail server's name; certificates are still verified and the password is never sent in clear text
* No change to opendesk itself; it is still at upstream commit 809b80d

[0.2.3]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit 06ac9a9
* Notify on new tickets and unassigned replies by email and in the browser, and show when each address last received mail
* Let Ollie find and change resources through the API, with improved approval cards and long-text display
* Keep verified STARTTLS for platform email, the pinned Cloudron base, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support unchanged

[0.2.4]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit 7def3c4
* Import older Collab mail on request with resumable checkpoints, storage allowances and search across messages; improve Gmail and Microsoft sync resumption
* Add per-address and mailbox-alias signatures, richer mail details, conversation history and French agent translations
* Include upstream reply undo and deletion markers, credential-key rotation support, backup checksums and support-channel workflow improvements
* Keep verified STARTTLS, the pinned Cloudron base, all four Cloudron patches, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support unchanged

[0.2.5]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit 9cc0b4f
* Let members answer email tickets from their own Collab addresses, with per-mailbox rules, a chosen Reply-To and replies brought back to the ticket
* Let Ollie ask a teammate's Ollie about mail the teammate chose to share, with consent and audience controls
* Improve admin session resilience and include upstream brand assets for email signatures
* Keep verified STARTTLS, the pinned Cloudron base, all four Cloudron patches, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support unchanged

[0.2.6]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit f38d6f7
* Add ticket panels for Shopify customer details and recent orders, or workspace-provided sections from a signed URL
* Include cross-workspace Spaces, an internal team wiki, public help-center changelogs, per-agent reports and German agent translations
* Show My tickets under each mail account, let members turn off a team's notifications, preview reply signatures and complete emails, and choose a 12-hour or 24-hour clock
* Include Front imports, Google Chat support, mailbox sync improvements, richer ticket filters and automation actions
* Include upstream trust-boundary hardening and fixes for malformed email CSS, inbound NUL bytes and import source links
* Keep verified STARTTLS, the pinned Cloudron base, all four Cloudron patches (forwarding patch context refreshed, behaviour unchanged), SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support

[0.2.7]
* Security: update the realtime gateway's web server, Bandit, from 1.13.1 to 1.14.1, fixing HTTP/1.1 chunked-body memory amplification, chunk-extension request smuggling and WebSocket fragment and close handling, plus several HTTP/2 issues
* Security: update the realtime gateway's JOSE library from 1.11.12 to 1.11.13, fixing eight advisories
* Security: the realtime gateway now listens only on 127.0.0.1, so other apps on the Cloudron internal network can no longer connect to it directly; browsers still reach it through the app's /socket path
* opendesk stays at upstream commit f38d6f7, and Cloudron patches 0001 to 0004 are unchanged

[0.2.8]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit 4440877
* Add a phone channel: connect Aircall so calls land on the caller's ticket, with call automations, call insight cards and click to call
* Offer AI drafts in the Collab composer, and let a Collab draft API key claim and draft waiting conversations for a person to send
* Group sidebar views into folding sections that can be pinned to Favorites, give each view an icon and colour, and duplicate views
* Let a workspace hide unused statuses from agents and give Send and solve its own button
* Add optional searchable ticket aliases, support-channel routing by priority and language-aware ticket panels
* Fix import syncs so they follow the source's ticket merges, label removals and customer moves
* Keep the pinned Cloudron base, all six Cloudron patches (unchanged), the loopback-only realtime gateway, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support

[0.2.9]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit a8bdb2a
* Add skill-based ticket routing with workspace skills, member assignments and routing-rule skill requirements
* Add a customer ticket portal for ticket history and replies
* Sync Gmail inbox categories in both directions and add Ollie summaries, suggested replies and warnings to support channels
* Open tickets, contacts and pages in new tabs through real links; optionally advance to the next ticket after sending and solving or closing
* Let a workspace disable agents' online-time tracking and delete previously recorded online time
* Include database migrations 000702 to 000705, applied automatically on start
* Keep the pinned Cloudron base, all six Cloudron patches (unchanged), verified STARTTLS, the loopback-only realtime gateway, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support

[0.2.10]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit 3bca4a0
* Let a Collab mail account default to Reply all for everyone answering from it, including shared conversations
* Optionally show editable ticket properties above the conversation, and remember ticket-list sort order per folder, view and team inbox
* Keep ticket panel cards folded or open across refreshes and updated answers
* Fix focused-button keyboard handling and keep a newly opened ticket at its latest message until the agent scrolls up
* Include database migration 000706, applied automatically on start; iPhone builds are not part of this package
* Keep the pinned Cloudron base, all six Cloudron patches (unchanged), verified STARTTLS, the loopback-only realtime gateway, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support

[0.2.11]
* Link the Community Apps Package button to this package's repository
* Requires Cloudron 10.0.0 or later; Cloudron 9 servers can no longer read this catalog
* No change to opendesk itself; it is still at upstream commit 3bca4a0

[0.2.12]
* The Community Apps Package link now opens this repository. The listing builds that link from packagerUrl, so the 0.2.11 packageUrl change had no visible effect.
* No change to opendesk itself; it is still at upstream commit 3bca4a0.

