[0.2.22]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit b761cc8
* Customers can sign in to a brand's help center through the brand's own identity provider, and start requests with a subject, a message and attached files; admins can merge two contacts, label, move or delete several at once, and filter People, Companies and Members
* Live chat: returning visitors see their open chats first, chats can go to one available teammate with a pop-up, links in replies get short labels, and the team sees whether the visitor is still on the page; saved replies can add labels, move or assign the ticket; view sections get icons and drag and drop
* Faster ticket search, optional ticket numbers left out of customer email subjects, and Voys call summaries and transcripts that arrive with a status
* Include database migrations 000738 to 000744, applied automatically on start; iPhone builds are not part of this package
* Keep the pinned Cloudron base, all five Cloudron patches unchanged, verified STARTTLS, the loopback-only realtime gateway, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support

[0.2.21]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit ce0ff21
* Contacts can have several email addresses, so mail from a work and a private address lands on one contact; agents' unsent replies are saved on the server and follow them to another device; a Ready for review box lists conversations with an AI draft waiting for a person
* First run asks whether a workspace is a shared inbox, a help desk or both; a shared mail account can start with no one added; Mail, Pages and settings keep loading while Tickets is off
* The chat widget can be restyled with documented CSS variables, the API can record a ticket message as the customer's own, and a company can be created from a contact's Company field
* Include database migrations 000732 and 000733, applied automatically on start; iPhone builds are not part of this package
* Keep the pinned Cloudron base, all five Cloudron patches unchanged, verified STARTTLS, the loopback-only realtime gateway, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support

[0.2.20]
* Update opendesk to upstream commit 82525df
* New Pages product beside Tickets and Mail: docs, databases and canvases on the wiki's engine, edited together live, with comments, links, templates and import and export; on by default and switched per workspace under Settings, Pages
* The wiki grows into a full workspace and members can arrange their own sidebar; wiki pages can embed players and documents from YouTube, Vimeo, Loom, Figma, Google, Miro and similar services
* Include database migrations 000720 to 000730, applied automatically on start; iPhone builds are not part of this package
* Post-install message and setup guide: the admin panel signs in with email, an opendesk password and a two-factor code, so a Cloudron sign-in account turns on two-factor and sets a password with Forgot password first; revoke an admin who leaves with opendesk-cli admin revoke, since that password works without Cloudron
* Keep the pinned Cloudron base, all five Cloudron patches unchanged, verified STARTTLS, the loopback-only realtime gateway, SSO, mailbox routing and help-center domain support
